# The zero-records refusal: a data file yielding no records used to
# complete "successfully", leaving a matrix whose variables pointed at
# nothing; ANY next command touching it crashed (observed session 39
# by tools/fuzz_parm.py, which mutates documented options over passing
# seed cases).  nvar now refuses cleanly, and the previously crashing
# sequence runs to a normal end.
nvar(dfile=empty.dat, A[4.0]=c1, B[4.0]=c2);
dstat;
